# veda/ — the official .veda open-source specification repository

- `README.md` — the complete specification, benefits, real-world examples, and community guidelines
- `LICENSE` — official MIT open-source license
- `pyproject.toml` — python packaging metadata to make veda-check pip-installable
- `examples/` — physical sandbox demonstrating multi-layered frontend and backend .veda indices
- `tests/` — automated verification tools and continuous integration scripts
- `.veda` — this self-documenting index mapping the repository's files
- `.gitignore` — standard ignore rules to keep OS/IDE junk out of the repository
